# Elgato Stream Deck (0fd9:006d) — hide from libinput.
#
# The Stream Deck is exposed by hid-generic as an evdev keyboard that emits a
# continuous stream of KEY_UNKNOWN. Two consequences in a Wayland session:
#
#   - idle never settles, so screensaver and lock timers never fire
#   - a physically held SUPER fires workspace switches in bursts
#
# Omarchy solved this inside the compositor:
#
#     hl.device({ name = "elgato-stream-deck", enabled = false })   -- hypr/input.lua
#
# Umbriel has no per-device disable. [[input.device]] accepts layout, variant,
# options, repeat_rate, repeat_delay, tap, disable_while_typing, click_method,
# natural_scroll, scroll_button, scroll_button_lock, accel_profile and
# sensitivity — but no `enabled`, which exists only under [input.tablet].
# Confirmed against the shipped config and the 106-action `umbriel msg` list.
#
# So the fix moves here, which is arguably where it always belonged: this is a
# kernel/evdev quirk, not a compositor concern, and a udev rule survives
# whatever compositor comes next.
#
# Only SUBSYSTEM=="input" is masked. The Stream Deck's control software speaks
# hidraw, a different subsystem, so nothing is lost.
#
# IDs verified on caesar via `udevadm info -a -n /dev/input/event2`:
#   ATTRS{idVendor}=="0fd9"  ATTRS{idProduct}=="006d"  ATTRS{product}=="Stream Deck"
# Re-verify before assuming these carry to another unit or a different model.

SUBSYSTEM=="input", ATTRS{idVendor}=="0fd9", ATTRS{idProduct}=="006d", ENV{LIBINPUT_IGNORE_DEVICE}="1"
